00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.020
that it allows you to
leverage the data at rest,

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.780
but protect that
data at rest using

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.950
a key that's under your
control in the Cloud KMS.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.640
And because of the work
that we did with Cloud HSM,

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.710
you can use both Cloud KMS and
Cloud HSM keys synonymously.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.050
OK, so you can actually use
this to actually protect data

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.475
with your keys in Cloud HSM.

00:02:04.475 --> 00:02:05.850
And then finally
we have customer

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.490
