00:33:30.822 --> 00:33:33.030
A few things we really hope
you take away today are--

00:33:33.030 --> 00:33:35.040
Cloud HSM allows simple
and scalable access

00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:37.263
to hardware-protected
keys, including inputting

00:33:37.263 --> 00:33:38.180
your own key material.

00:33:38.180 --> 00:33:39.975
Cloud KMS enables
easy management

00:33:39.975 --> 00:33:41.850
of all of your encryption
keys, regardless of

00:33:41.850 --> 00:33:43.560
whether or not
they're in an HSM.

00:33:43.560 --> 00:33:46.590
And then CMEK enables you to
control encryption across all--

00:33:46.590 --> 00:33:50.400
not all-- some GCP
services very simply

00:33:50.400 --> 00:33:51.810
to achieve your
compliance goals.

